    array.push(cH, "Hot US inflation and new US tariffs on Europe kept EURUSD's bearish read firmly in place.|Mann asked for hikes 'more and sooner' while US data ran hot, so cable's tension only grew.|Sticky US prices and a US tariff list that names Japan give USDJPY's bullish read extra room.|The franc won the risk-off day, but USDCHF's fundamental lean still points up.|Canada was spared from the new US tariff list, yet USDCAD's wide bullish gap barely flinched.|The Aussie's CPI pop faded by evening, but AUDUSD's comeback condition is still half met.|Risk-off weighed on the kiwi, but Monday's strong retail data still keep NZDUSD's call under pressure.|Two MPC hawks in two days tilt EURGBP's stand-off gently toward the pound.|Both Europe and Japan landed on the US tariff list, and the yen side could feel it more.|Fear sent money to the franc, and both sides of EURCHF picked up a tariff headline.|Hot Aussie inflation still has no RBA voice behind it, so EURAUD remains a watch.|A tariff headline for Europe and a risk-off day for the kiwi cancel out in EURNZD.|The tariff list hit Europe and spared Canada, yet EURCAD's bullish read still stands.|Hawkish MPC voices and a US tariff list naming Japan both lean GBPJPY bullish, if scored.|A haven rush helped the franc, but the BoE hawks give GBPCHF an upside scenario.|GBPAUD now has hawkish talk on one side and hot data on the other, still without a winner.|Mann's hawkish call pushes GBPNZD's story a step closer to a bullish read.|The tech sell-off met the pound's 'deeper equity rout' line, putting GBPCAD's bull case under pressure.|Hot Aussie CPI and a tariff list naming Japan both point AUDJPY higher, but only as scenarios.|The franc won the fear trade today, while the Aussie's CPI scenario is still waiting for the RBA.|Australia's inflation beat still gives AUDNZD a bullish scenario, even on a risk-off day.|Deeper risk-off met the Aussie's weakening line, so AUDCAD's bullish case is under pressure.|Risk-off hurt the kiwi, and the tariff list touched the yen: NZDJPY stays two-sided.|The franc's haven bid and the kiwi's risk-off pain keep NZDCHF close to bearish but not there.|Deeper risk-off met the kiwi's weakening line, putting NZDCAD's bullish call under pressure.|Monday's risk-on spark is gone, so CADJPY's bearish read is back on firmer ground.|The franc's haven bid returned in force, keeping CADCHF's bearish read on track.|Both havens landed on the US tariff list, so CHFJPY stays a stand-off.|Gold lost another 1–2% on hot core PCE, and XAUUSD's dollar condition is now half met.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED~Q3 GDP revised to 4.3% (cons 3.5%), core PCE 3.3% y/y vs 3.2%: R3 +2 (raw 7.65, held at +7); December hike priced in the mid-to-high 90s.|CONFIRMED (watch)~EU named in the US Section 301 tariff proposal (15% deal cap); N2 already −1; French CMP on Thursday.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Mann: hike 'more and sooner'; Lombardelli hawkish, Dhingra dovish; 81% priced (unverified); shadow +3 if R2 +1.|WEAKENED (watch)~Monday's risk-on condition reversed; Japan on the US tariff list (15% cap): shadow −3 if N2 +1 → 0; no MoF comment.|CONFIRMED (watch)~Haven winner; VIX 30–33 intraday (no close above 30 yet); Switzerland on the US tariff list: shadow −1 if N2 −1.|CONFIRMED (watch)~Canada not on the US tariff list; Brent $90–91; BoC pricing reports conflict (unverified).|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~CPI data half met, RBA silent; Dec hold 96.7%, May cut odds 48% from 56%; deeper risk-off also met the weakening line.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Carried: Q3 retail beat; risk-off met the NZDCAD weakening line intraday; election result Friday.|CONFIRMED (watch)~Gold −1.4% to −2.4% after PCE (price only); 10-year −6bp; XAUUSD dollar condition half met.")
