    array.push(cT, timestamp("Europe/Bucharest", 2026, 11, 26, 0, 0))
    array.push(cN, "Thu 26 Nov · morning")
    array.push(cD, "C-7,P-7,W8,C7,C14,P-7,P-9,W0,W1,T0,W0,T2,C7,W1,W0,W0,W2,S7,W1,W0,W2,S7,W-1,T-2,S5,S-6,C-7,T1,T1")
    array.push(cH, "Wall Street clawed back most of a 3% slide, and EURUSD's bearish read went into Thanksgiving untouched.|Bailey sounded a shade calmer than his hawkish colleagues, so cable's pressure tag holds but does not grow.|Tamura told Yamanashi that rates must reach neutral 'soon', and USDJPY's bullish read now has a yen to watch.|The VIX settled near 28 instead of above 30, so USDCHF's bullish lean keeps its footing.|Oil jumped 3.5% on a refinery attack claim, but USDCAD's fourteen-point gap shrugged it off.|A 12.2% surge in Australian business investment adds weight to the Aussie's comeback case against the dollar.|A quiet night for the kiwi leaves NZDUSD's pressure tag hanging on Friday's official count.|Bailey's softer tone and a French budget committee day keep EURGBP's stand-off balanced.|Tamura's call to reach neutral 'soon' gives EURJPY's quiet stand-off a yen-leaning scenario.|Fear faded into the close, and EURCHF stays a level fight on both sides.|Australia's capex boom stacks a second hot number on the Aussie side of EURAUD.|A silent kiwi and a busy euro calendar leave EURNZD where it started the week.|Oil's rebound gave the loonie a lift, yet EURCAD's bullish read is still intact.|Bailey eased the tone and Tamura sharpened his, so GBPJPY's two upside scenarios now face a downside one.|The haven rush cooled at the close, and GBPCHF keeps its pound-side scenario.|A capex boom on one side and a calmer Bailey on the other tilt GBPAUD's scenarios toward the Aussie.|GBPNZD drifts at +2 while the kiwi waits for Friday's count and the pound digests Bailey.|The equity rout did not deepen on the close, so GBPCAD's pressure tag lifts.|Hot Aussie investment meets a hawkish Tamura, and AUDJPY's scenarios now point both ways.|The capex surprise strengthens the Aussie's scenario as the franc's haven bid fades.|Australia keeps posting surprises while New Zealand stays silent, and AUDNZD's +6 scenario grows more plausible.|The risk-off did not deepen on the close and Aussie capex surged, so AUDCAD returns to 'could get even stronger'.|Tamura's hawkish turn gives NZDJPY a bearish scenario for the first time this week.|The franc's fear premium cooled, and NZDCHF stays just inside two-sided territory.|Wall Street's recovery removed the deeper risk-off threat, so NZDCAD's bullish read regains its footing.|Tamura's hawkish speech could make CADJPY's bearish read even stronger.|Oil helped the loonie, but CADCHF's bearish read is not threatened.|Tamura gives the yen a hawkish card, and CHFJPY's stand-off now has a scenario each way.|Falling Treasury yields gave gold a softer backdrop, but XAUUSD's gold factor is unchanged.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED~Fed still 97% for December, January 63%; Beige Book growth in 8 of 12 districts; R3 +2 shadow carried (raw 7.65, held at +7).|CONFIRMED (watch)~French PLFSS joint committee and ECB accounts today; no scored input overnight.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Carried from Greene/Mann; Bailey hinted inflation may peak lower if energy settles (single report); shadow +3 if R2 +1.|WEAKENED (watch)~Tamura: reach neutral ( 2%) 'soon', no explicit December pledge; shadow +2 if R2 0, −3 with the tariff scenario.|CONFIRMED (watch)~VIX closed near 28 after topping 30 intraday: neither the 30 nor the 25 line met on a close; tariff scenario −1.|CONFIRMED (watch)~Brent +3.5% to $94.61 on a Houthi refinery claim (N1 information only); no written loonie trigger met.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Carried (CPI); Q3 capex +12.2% vs 4.4% expected adds to the data line; RBA still silent; shadow +4 if R2 +1.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Carried from the Q3 retail beat; no NZ news overnight; official election result Friday.|CONFIRMED (watch)~10-year down to 4.80% in Asia (real-yield relief, information); gold closes conflict; G +1 unchanged.")
